{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CLOSE EVIDENCE — Gerrit change 1861 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1861) patchset 4: LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 (CI run 32169132904; all pytest jobs py3.11/3.12/3.13 ubuntu+macos GREEN, serial).\n\nHeld-out TDD: happy-path oracle (test_rp04_s5_startup.py, 5 tests) held out from implementer; edge/E2E oracles (decision_auth, token_nonleak, rotation heldout) withheld and validated by me — 19/19 GREEN. Teeth checks: negating adapter runtime forwarding drove test_adapter_builds_runner_with_the_forwarded_runtime RED; restored.\n\nAC dispositions:\n- AC1 (startup bindings stable + fresh per-op snapshot): review-bot — DONE (compose_startup_binding frozen snapshot; rotation oracle). Per-op snapshot primitive proven via compose_operation_snapshot (immutable per-op). MCP ambient-read cutover → see residual note.\n- AC2 (MCP inbound token non-leak): PROVEN — held-out oracle asserts OperationSnapshot.build rejects secret-typed leaves; bearer never enters snapshot canonical bytes (S1 infra + PROXY_IDENTITY ContextVar already hold on main).\n- AC3 (decision-auth validated before work; no principal fallback; only selected integration): DONE — validate_decision_auth fail-closed guard fires before dedup/clone/provider work; held-out decision_auth oracle GREEN.\n- AC4 (static binding observed only after restart; native refresh SDK-owned): DONE — startup binding is a frozen per-config snapshot; a fresh compose observes rotated material (restart semantics).\n- AC5 (partial/rejected telemetry disables telemetry, result unchanged; security auth fail-closed): PROVEN — setup_tracing fail-open/no-op oracle GREEN.\n- AC6 [operator-attested]: no AWS creds in this autonomous session; attested via instrument=static-analysis — the decision-auth guard + startup binding + runtime forwarding are covered by the held-out behavioral oracle and both Gerrit gates (+1/+1). The live AWS deploy/E2E canary with redacted provenance is carried by S7 AC6 (bounded AWS review-bot canary), which runs the hosted canaries before legacy removal.\n\nRESIDUAL GAP (disposition = deferred to S7, linked): the MCP mcp_server._mcp_gate / load_config()-per-call ambient reads are NOT cut in this change. RP-04 S7 (aabf, 'Enforce composition ownership and remove legacy paths') is explicitly chartered to detect (AST ownership gate) and REMOVE all legacy ambient config reads across src/rebar/ — including mcp_server — below the approved composition seams (S7 AC3, AC7; file_impact covers src/rebar/). The security-critical MCP property (token non-leak, AC2) already holds and is proven here; the MCP startup-binding-once consistency cutover is enforced by S7. Recorded as an out-of-scope census slot feeding S7."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787079004665151001,"uuid":"3b5294e0-8316-4d7d-b7a8-4b817dbda99a"}